Package: vosa
Type: Package
Title: Variance-Optimized Saliences Analysis for Multiblock Data
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-11-25
Authors@R: c(
    person("Saida", "Ballah Houssein", role = "aut"),
    person("Jean-Michel", "Galharret", role = "aut"),
    person("Mohamed", "Hanafi", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mohamed.hanafi@oniris-nantes.fr"))
Description: Exploratory multiblock dimension reduction based on block
    saliences, the share of each block's inertia reproduced by a common
    component. Implements the family of criteria
    g_alpha = (1 - alpha) * level^2 + alpha * contrast, which contains CPCA
    (alpha = 0), orthogonal INDSCAL / INDORT (alpha = 1/2, the simultaneous
    version of ComDim / CCSWA) and VOSA (alpha = 1), the method that maximizes
    the variance of the saliences of a component. All criteria are computed
    with the Shifted Polar Ascent (SPA) algorithm, whose monotone ascent is
    guaranteed for indefinite blocks. STATIS is provided for comparison.
    Results can be returned in the canonical factorization
    X_k = U D_k V_k' + E_k common to multiblock methods. Diagnostics include
    the rho ratio, the relative bounds on the contrast gain, the heterogeneity
    of block structures and the comparison with block principal components.
